SofaCUDA (SOFA v25.12): RigidMapping<Rigid3,CudaVec3f>::applyJT maps surface forces to a
wrong torque. After its reduction, RigidMappingCuda3f_applyJT_kernel writes temp[0..5], but
the torque sums are at temp[3*BSIZE .. 3*BSIZE+2]; temp[3..5] are thread 1's partial forces.
A rigid body whose surface receives forces then turns the wrong way (found and checked in
this project; see README section 9.11). Apply from the SOFA source root:
    patch -p1 < SofaCUDA-RigidMapping-applyJT-torque.patch

--- a/applications/plugins/SofaCUDA/src/SofaCUDA/component/mapping/nonlinear/CudaRigidMapping.cu
+++ b/applications/plugins/SofaCUDA/src/SofaCUDA/component/mapping/nonlinear/CudaRigidMapping.cu
@@ -192,7 +192,9 @@
     __syncthreads();
     if (index1 < 6)
     {
-        out[blockIdx.x * 6 + index1] = temp[index1];
+        // Thread 0 holds the block's force sum in temp[0..2] and its torque sum in
+        // temp[3*BSIZE .. 3*BSIZE+2]; temp[3..5] are thread 1's partial forces.
+        out[blockIdx.x * 6 + index1] = index1 < 3 ? temp[index1] : temp[3 * BSIZE + index1 - 3];
     }
 }
 
